{"schemaVersion":"1.0.0","kind":"eigenquestions-fine-index","destinations":[{"id":"source-question:0d7140e5f635bf81dc422fcc83eecdfe6f05646ba420b3c6ba16a75c39d0ee74","title":"Can increasing quantized flux produce controlled supersymmetric vacua with a mass gap between every modulus and the AdS curvature scale? The paper tests whether the flux freedom that controls an expansion also forces some scalar Compton wavelengths to remain comparable to the AdS radius.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0001"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:0d81c4d10f58df1b7b2ddf37c8f21fd3e4bb1c5ed77d081808fa0dbd5dee917e","title":"Which Calabi–Yau geometries admit nonsupersymmetric AdS minima at exponentially large volume, and when can string loops qualitatively complete Kähler-modulus stabilisation rather than merely perturb an existing minimum?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0005"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:0de5de8251f489f0078986971d85b68c64333788ec3812e7d7da57cbdc46ab1e","title":"What restrictions does four-dimensional accelerated expansion impose on higher-dimensional compactifications, including the evolution of moduli and the distribution and time dependence of NEC-violating sources?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0006"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:0d86ee83335cba2f44d57a6fd585405baf97660f9ccba1d20f42ef24e94afedc","title":"Can vector bundle moduli provide sufficient F-term uplift to stabilize supersymmetry-breaking Minkowski or de Sitter vacua in heterotic M-theory, including when the tree-level superpotential is constant?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0007"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:0dbfcfe74c2c22b440ba188b55524a83290e93b0bf26ff94aaa457b43e5ba3c0","title":"What theoretical and epistemic status should local and averaged energy conditions have, given their powerful geometric consequences, interpretive difficulties, and physically important violations? How might they constrain alternative spacetime theories?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0016"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:0de926982a3e0f6935b165bf94f93a2c1f1f70a001184481db4b38c51c737388","title":"How do anomaly cancellation and α′ corrections constrain heterotic compactification moduli, which tangent-connection deformations represent physical fields, and can torsion or NS flux support geometric stabilization when four-dimensional maximal symmetry is relaxed?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0017"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:0dd7afc4b7841f50fadfb82cd3a194cc7b24833683d82a477c7622e4371f09da","title":"Do the WGC and gravitational instantons exclude super-Planckian fundamental-domain diameters, and hence large-field inflation without monodromy, in theories with many axions?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0018"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:0d86c0948f6601a0b14f2130d02eeff6ce376a9dc113bf20efb18ac4c52d8b0e","title":"How do branes, orientifolds, intersections, and fluxes generate four-dimensional gauge sectors and chiral matter?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0027"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:0de0ad84cc807325ec2f6cc317736a86dd4606d0d3fc825a741c23cd20332c97","title":"Can type-IIB string theory realize a parametrically light massive AdS4 graviton, and can its mass be expressed using only effective bag gravity, throat D3 charges, and dilaton jumps?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0029"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:0dd6aed464c34eb985dde90983f24a4c98f757c57c4375844dc860084e84a420","title":"Does Coleman's α integration remain consistent when higher-curvature couplings and Wilsonian running are included? The FKS setup adds an R² coupling to the cosmological and Einstein terms.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0030"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:0d295ccd3b43313998600e4d734f992c6b88e64a801f7acf1c0fc8d482fe99bd","title":"Can positive-energy 4D FLRW cosmology and effective gravity emerge on an expanding decay bubble in AdS, without requiring a fundamental de Sitter vacuum or a scale-separated compactification?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0030"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:0d984ab259ff05da671c13b38119b694e910527e64198b0501347b5108d9f9da","title":"Does the simplest single-modulus KKLT construction admit a controlled warped anti-D3 uplift to de Sitter, assuming gaugino condensation has a ten-dimensional description, and can four-dimensional supergravity parametrizations encode the authors’ proposed obstruction?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0033"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:0d5436f249a3d0078bd569dee6ad68e178bb73df7292e15d79287450bc87225d","title":"Review how interacting renormalization-group fixed points can provide predictive ultraviolet completions for matter and gravity, and whether gravity–matter interactions could connect Planck-scale dynamics to observable particle physics.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0034"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:0de09fc89be45aa7aed25bbcdc28100471fa55c8fc0f8ca8e3601ac41f6a3d12","title":"Which proposed solutions forbid the supersymmetric μ term and regenerate |μ| near 100–300 GeV while accommodating multi-TeV soft breaking, and which also address axion quality, neutrino masses or experimentally distinguishable signatures?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0039"},"indexTemplate":"so