ing the distance conjecture and strong emergence, do tower-induced one-loop kinetic terms and potentials destabilize an initially positive-energy de Sitter configuration, and how does tower statistics affect the answer?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0082"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:0df096ada3b37c5c4a04754a35b9f5604783ed8130e6e9fbde8c0fdd52a84ddb","title":"How does bulk radiation initially hotter than the compactification scale induce oscillations of stabilized moduli, alter three-dimensional expansion, and determine transitions between radiation and moduli domination?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0086"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:0d1ff9c0b6f631044bc4bd1e38fc39aa5a51175434faf15e5047155617a49854","title":"Can quantized fluxes in the 2^6 Landau–Ginzburg orientifold stabilize all moduli in supersymmetric Minkowski vacua, including fields with zero quadratic mass, while satisfying tadpole cancellation?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0089"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:0de1514083e5d30da52fdef98cdf24e5c6352b6d463b29ec77b284c942fa4946","title":"Can one fixed holographic CFT state have two simple semiclassical bulk descriptions differing by the presence of a closed universe? Which bulk-boundary dictionary and inner product then describe an observer's experience?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0089"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:0d945ea17b4b68627594445073b73c0a5ca439892f131fa406d390109d981c00","title":"What charges, stability properties, and near-horizon worldsheet descriptions characterize non-supersymmetric heterotic 0-, 4-, 6-, and 7-branes, and how are their angular theories detected by Green–Schwarz couplings and related to topological modular forms?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-deta