resent each massive vacuum, and reproduce its asymptotic-state scales and global symmetries?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0107"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:0d3432d9d4e89d28ba038c6c7b9ae6a44ca2555a198aa679b4616504d54e17aa","title":"Can analytic continuation of known DBI brane excitations produce time-dependent configurations analogous to gravitational bubbles and S-branes, and illuminate brane–antibrane annihilation?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0109"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:0df3969aa06b524142ea55a0fac85752f8496cc9ca569eee218bd0c6acce8e5c","title":"Can stationary spacetimes admit a thermodynamically meaningful volume independent of stationary slicing, and can discrete identifications produce bounded horizon area with unbounded volume? The latter question motivates a conditional discussion of the statistical interpretation of black-hole entropy.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0114"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:0d89e6397a2ab1feb8eef826a3ef2e8cb008a19b4aa6a707a6f4ae2ad2f499f8","title":"Can heterotic compactification guided by local SO(10) unification produce the MSSM spectrum, decouple exotic matter consistently with supersymmetry, and accommodate realistic Yukawa couplings and hidden-sector supersymmetry breaking?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0115"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:0d88753b5f19ae4e81ad094b46ae181445c5c32fd6bcdc9f0b839e5fbe5b513f","title":"Can a black hole assist a process that converts heat completely into work and thereby violates the second law?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0121"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"}],"relations":[{"id":"source-access:683cc886faba314f23b2fe83","source":"q025-placement-question:96bd49b710515fe2e5ef12ae","target":"sou